[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write up a clean proof.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe answer is **No**. We provide a counterexample.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet $A = \ell^\infty(\mathbb{N})$, the $C^*$-algebra of bounded complex-valued [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msequences. This is a unital commutative $C^*$-algebra (with pointwise operations[0m[38;2;124;124;124mand the sup norm).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**$A$ is non-separable:** For each subset $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, let $\chi_S [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\in \ell^\infty(\mathbb{N})$ be the characteristic function of $S$. There are [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$2^{\aleph_0}$ such subsets. For distinct subsets $S \neq T$, we have $\|\chi_S [0m[38;2;124;124;124m- \chi_T\|_\infty = 1$. Thus $\ell^\infty(\mathbb{N})$ contains an uncountable [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfamily of elements at pairwise distance 1, which means no countable dense subset[0m[38;2;124;124;124mcan exist. Hence $A$ is non-separable.[0m

